e given route.\n     *\n     * Resolves `activeIndex` by matching the tab button's `route` rather than hardcoding a position, so\n     * the controller stays correct when the `items` array is reordered.\n     *\n     * The lookup MUST use `getTabBar().items` (the header buttons), NOT `component.items`:\n     * `Neo.tab.Container.createItems()` transforms the user `items` into `[HeaderToolbar, Strip,\n     * BodyContainer]`, so the original `item.header.route` is gone at route time. The header buttons\n     * survive that transform and carry both `route` (a `Neo.button.Base` config) and `index` (the\n     * original tab index the engine also reads on click).\n     * @param {String} route\n     */","meta":{"range":[2078,2254],"filename":"TabContainerController.mjs","lineno":47,"columnno":4,"path":"/Users/tobiasuhlig/.neo-ai/agents/neo-gpt-emmy/neomjs/pages/node_modules/neo.mjs/apps/portal/view/news","code":{"id":"astnode100002587","name":"TabContainerController#activateRoute","type":"MethodDefinition","paramnames":["route"]},"vars":{"":null},"srcPath":"apps/portal/view/news/TabContainerController.mjs"},"summary":"Activates the tab whose header button carries the given route.\n\nResolves `activeIndex` by matching the tab button's `route` rather than hardcoding a position, so\nthe controller stays correct when the `items` array is reordered.\n\nThe lookup MUST use `getTabBar().items` (the header buttons), NOT `component.items`:\n`Neo.tab.Container.createItems()` transforms the user `items` into `[HeaderToolbar, Strip,\nBodyContainer]`, so the original `item.header.route` is gone at route time. The header buttons\nsurvive that transform and carry both `route` (a `Neo.button.Base` config) and `index` (the\noriginal tab index the engine also reads on click).","params":[{"type":{"names":["String"]},"name":"route"}],"name":"activateRoute","longname":"TabContainerController#activateRoute","kind":"function","memberof":"TabContainerController","scope":"instance","$longname":"Ta